    "exit_rule": "container above the bowl and upright with no particle in the bowl at the final state",
    "guidance": "**Secondary candidate for phase-ambiguous nominal entries.** This bowl-frame policy with causal phase supervision met the full stage exit in 7/12 validation runs (58.3%). Every run ended upright with zero particles in the bowl, but 5/12 failed because the container was not over the bowl. All runs had zero IK-unconverged steps. Prefer its documented niche when entering near demonstrated approach, just after closure, or already lifted and the grasp/lift phase is ambiguous; use h04 instead when a broadly stronger validated exit rate is desired.\n\nRequire finite container/bowl poses and corroborate phase using finger width, source elevation, and source/TCP co-motion. Avoid for a strongly displaced ungrasped source, large source/bowl rotations, noisy or reordered phase observations, missed grasps, slips, changed geometry, obstacles, or unreachable targets. These cases are unsupported, and no out-of-distribution phase-recovery result exists.\n\nFailure is most directly recognized when the source remains upright but does not reach the bowl footprint, matching all five validation failures. Also stop for phase inference inconsistent with finger/elevation/co-motion evidence, closed fingers without source motion, drop, early particle escape, IK nonconvergence, or limit contact. The auxiliary phase class is not contact evidence.\n\nHand off to `controlled_pour_and_right` only on observed closure, source/TCP co-motion, table clearance, upright high staging over the bowl, and no particle in the bowl; never hand off merely because the phase head indicates “lifted.”"
  },
